  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "What is the product of all positive odd integers less than \\(10{,}000?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{10000!}{(5000!)^2}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{10000!}{2^{5000}}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{9999!}{2^{5000}}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{10000!}{2^{5000} \\cdot 5000!}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{5000!}{2^{5000}}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A factorial includes all the consecutive positive integers up to its argument: \\(n!=1\\cdot2\\cdots n\\). This lets us obtain the desired odd product by removing the even factors from \\(10000!\\).\n\nLet \\(P=1\\cdot3\\cdot5\\cdots9999\\). Every factor in \\(10000!\\) is either one of these odd numbers or an even number, so\n\\[\n10000!=P(2\\cdot4\\cdot6\\cdots10000).\n\\]\nThere are \\(5000\\) even factors, each contributing a factor of \\(2\\). Thus\n\\[\n2\\cdot4\\cdots10000\n=2^{5000}(1\\cdot2\\cdots5000)\n=2^{5000}\\cdot5000!.\n\\]\nDividing by this positive product gives\n\\[\nP=\\boxed{\\frac{10000!}{2^{5000}\\cdot5000!}},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
